  "low_vol_growth_rotation": {
    "name": "low_vol_growth_rotation",
    "description": "Goes long XLK (tech/growth) and short XLV/XLP (defensive healthcare+staples) when SPY's 21-day realized volatility is below its 252-day average by more than half a standard deviation. Flat otherwise. Position size: +0.5 XLK, -0.25 XLV, -0.25 XLP. Rebalances daily when vol regime changes.",
    "hypothesis": "In low-volatility equity regimes, investors rotate toward growth/tech (XLK) and away from defensive sectors (XLV, XLP), because: (1) low vol = risk-on environment where yield-seeking defensive attributes are penalized; (2) tech earnings are more sensitive to growth expectations, which are elevated in calm markets; (3) defensives carry a volatility premium that gets compressed in calm periods. The signal is adaptive \u2014 it goes flat whenever vol spikes, naturally cutting risk during drawdown environments. This is the equity-side analog of the VIX risk premium.",
    "universe_size": 4,
